Thanks for the response;

Regarding the new benchmark governance section: this is a good addition, but why not describe the "structured governance program"? The sentences that follow seem to pertain to releases only; who dictates what data goes where, and who has access to it? What 3rd-parties can access the private dataset? What does it mean that "We also encourage automated attack generation to sustain the benchmark’s robustness and longevity."?

Regarding the attack diversity analysis: I feel like some numbers are missing here; how many submissions did you start with? How many were left after the exact/near-deduplication? Isn't using an LLM here a bit dangerous given how sensitive they are to some attack prompts? Thanks for the details on the strategies though, that seems quite interesting, I will be eager to see the final version.

